# Scope-only Nexus routing: only @petedio packages route to Nexus npm-hosted.
# Public packages (express, pino, zod, etc.) fall through to the default
# npm registry (npmjs.org) — which means bun.lock pins public URLs that
# CI runners can reach without VPN / Cloudflare tunnel auth.
#
# Why this matters: the publish workflow uses BUN_CONFIG_REGISTRY=npmjs.org
# to override at install time, but --frozen-lockfile follows lockfile URLs
# literally. If the lockfile is generated against a Nexus-default config,
# every transitive dep gets pinned to registry.pdlab.dev and CI can't
# fetch them (502s / Cloudflare timeouts from external runners).
#
# Mirrors the .npmrc pattern in services/ollama-gateway/ and the agent repos.
# Auth value injected from NEXUS_AUTH env var at install time when present;
# anonymous Nexus reads work for @petedio scope without it (cosmetic warning).
@petedio:registry=https://registry.pdlab.dev/repository/npm-hosted/
//registry.pdlab.dev/repository/npm-hosted/:_auth=${NEXUS_AUTH}
